\par \pard\li175 \f4\cf1 
\par \b Standard\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is the cheapest armor available.
\par \b Trinnium\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 more effective than Standard armor, particularly against cannon and missile attacks. 
\par \b Assault\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is Trinnium armor that is better designed to protect against frontal attacks; rear protection does suffer.
\par \b Didrate\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 more effective than Trinnium armor particularly against plasma-based attacks. 
\par \b Tri-di\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 more effective than Didrate armor; also particularly effective against plasma-based attacks.
\par \pard\li175 \b Improved 8.6cm Assault\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is Tri-di armor that is better designed to protect against frontal attacks; rear protection does suffer.
\par \b Antiballistic Coat\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 allows extreme agility and good protection against cannon attacks.
\par \b Advanced Heat Differential\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 more effective than Didrate armor; also allows extreme agility and good protection against plasma attacks.
\par \b Crystalline Mesh\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 diffuses laser-based attacks extremely well. Much less effective against other attacks. 
\par \pard\li175 \b Liquid Tri\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 more effective than Tri-di armor.
\par \b Heavy Assault\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 weighted Liquid-Tri armor; better designed to protect against frontal attacks; rear protection does suffer.
\par \b Clearplast\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 extremely effective against all attacks except lasers.
\par 
\par Numbers indicate armor rating, based on the deflective and ablative capabilities of the armor; a blank slot means the Herc is not capable of carrying that armor.
